// Skip mode (2026-08-10): eliminated players are never offered prompts and
// their remaining instructions are skipped (only `cycle to next` still
// runs). The `score 1 to P:P1` line sits *between* the elimination and the
// cycle, so it is skipped once the current player is out — P1 never scores.
// When no players remain in the game, the stage auto-ends with an empty
// winner set. The optional is therefore offered exactly twice — P1 and P2 —
// never to an out-of-game player, and the 10-iteration cap is never reached.
player P1, P2
turnorder (P:P1, P:P2)
location Hand on all
location Deck on table

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Two)

stage Play for current 10 times {
  optional {
    deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    set current out of game
  }
  score 1 to P:P1
  cycle to next
}
